Title of the Paper: Morphometric analysis of the pancreas in diabetes mellitus patients.
Abstract of the Paper: A description is given of the electron microscopic-morphometric findings obtained for the islets of Langerhans of the pancreas and for the glucagon-producing ? cells of one patient suffering from longstanding insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (IDDM, type I diabetes), two patients with longstanding insulin-independent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM, type II diabetes), and one non-diabetic. The study examines structural changes in the pancreas associated with diabetes mellitus and its subtypes.
Entity Information:
- { "id": "C0030274", "name": "pancreas", "pos": [118, 126] }
- { "id": "C0011849", "name": "diabetes mellitus", "pos": [325, 342] }

Title of the Paper: Incidence of Diabetes Mellitus and Impaired Glucose Tolerance Following Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.
Abstract of the Paper: We undertook this study to determine the incidence of diabetes mellitus (DM) and impaired glucose tolerance (IGT) after gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM). The objective was to examine whether individuals with a history of GDM have an increased risk of developing DM or IGT later in life.
